From 03a6e2c14c5cd80e7d72f257539cf6c807187a40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devbotbo <7118.eth@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:55:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add verifier mode for the bridge: POST /request with a caller
 nonce, GET /result/:id with the presentation

The bridge needs the nonce to be sha256(address || challenge) and needs the
raw SD-JWT presentation afterwards to prove the statement. Both are read-side
additions to the default path:

- bridge.rs: nonce validation (16 to 128 chars of [A-Za-z0-9_-]) and a session
  table that refuses a nonce while another session with it is pending (409)
  and reports pending for sessions created this way.
- SessionResult::Verified now keeps the presentation string exactly as it came
  out of the decrypted vp_token, beside the parsed VerifiedPid. Gated by
  RESULT_INCLUDES_PRESENTATION (default true); off keeps only the summary.
- create_request takes the nonce; the landing page still passes a UUID.
- POST /request returns 201 with both naming conventions (session/session_id,
  authorization_request/openid4vp_uri) and result_url; GET /result/:id answers
  pending | verified (+ presentation, verified_pid) | rejected (+ error).
- A bridge session's optional redirect_uri is returned to the wallet on a
  verified POST. GET /zk/result/:id and the relay path are unchanged.
---
